<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Motion Prompt and Temporal Embedding.</span>
Both motion prompts and temporal position embedding improve temporal consistency and semantic coherence, as shown in Tab. <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 4.3 Ablation Studies &amp; Model Analysis ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SAMPO: Scale-wise Autoregression with Motion PrOmpt for generative world models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Particularly, temporal position embedding plays a crucial role in maintaining consistent temporal dynamics, resulting in significant improvements in FVD and SSIM.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.15536v1/zero-shot.png" id="S4.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/67;" width="476" height="67" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span><span id="S4.F6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Zero-shot performance.</span> The results show that SAMPO can effectively generalize without special design and finetuning, underscoring its potential for world models. Zoom in for a better view.</figcaption>
</figure>
