<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tokenizer.</span> In the proposed asymmetric multi-scale tokenizer, we adopt a hierarchical design to balance spatial detail preservation and computational efficiency <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite>. As detailed in Tab. <a href="#A1.T6" title="Table A ‣ A.1 Details of Network ‣ Appendix A Implementation Details ‣ SAMPO: Scale-wise Autoregression with Motion PrOmpt for generative world models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>, for observed frames (<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>), dense tokenization is applied across all spatial scales
<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{full}=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{full}=10</annotation></semantics></math>. For future frames (<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>), a sparse subset of coarser scales <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{full}=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{full}=6</annotation></semantics></math> is used, focusing on dynamic regions while minimizing redundancy <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>.
Both observed and future frames use a codebook size of 8192 with an embedding dimension of 64.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Transformer.</span> The SAMPO transformer utilizes a scalable decoder-only architecture, inspired by GPT-2, to efficiently model spatiotemporal dynamics.
Unlike iVideoGPT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite>, which relies on specialized tokens for frame segmentation, we initialize each frame with a single start token <span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[S]</span>. This token serves a dual function: it marks the beginning of intra-frame autoregressive generation and naturally defines the temporal boundaries between consecutive frames. Fixed 1D sine-cosine positional embeddings are applied to encode temporal dynamics, following standard practices in vision Transformers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>, <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite>. We design a set of models with different sizes, as illustrated in Tab. <a href="#A1.T7" title="Table B ‣ A.1 Details of Network ‣ Appendix A Implementation Details ‣ SAMPO: Scale-wise Autoregression with Motion PrOmpt for generative world models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>.
Model scaling adheres to a linear relationship between depth <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, width <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, head count <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, and dropout rate <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dr</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=64d,\quad\quad h=d,\quad\quad dr=0.1\cdot d/24." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=64d,\quad\quad h=d,\quad\quad dr=0.1\cdot d/24.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Details of Training</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training setup.</span> Tab. <a href="#A1.T8" title="Table C ‣ A.1 Details of Network ‣ Appendix A Implementation Details ‣ SAMPO: Scale-wise Autoregression with Motion PrOmpt for generative world models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a> summarizes the hyperparameters used in SAMPO across datasets. Training proceeds via uniform segment sampling with dataset-specific step sizes (see Tab. <a href="#A1.T9" title="Table D ‣ A.2 Details of Training ‣ Appendix A Implementation Details ‣ SAMPO: Scale-wise Autoregression with Motion PrOmpt for generative world models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>), where step lengths are tuned to match each dataset’s native temporal frequency. For tokenizer training, we use the initial observed frames as context, while the transformer is trained on full-length sequences.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Scale-specific weight.</span>
The scale-specific weight <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In 3.4 Training Objectives ‣ 3 Method ‣ SAMPO: Scale-wise Autoregression with Motion PrOmpt for generative world models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) balances the contribution of each spatial scale to the total loss. Given a multi-scale tokenizer with patch sizes <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{patch}=[1,...,L_{K}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{patch}=[1,...,L_{K}]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\texttt{len}(L_{patch})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">len</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\texttt{len}(L_{patch})</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of spatial scales, <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{l}=\frac{L_{l}^{2}}{\sum_{k=1}^{K}L_{k}^{2}}\cdot K." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{l}=\frac{L_{l}^{2}}{\sum_{k=1}^{K}L_{k}^{2}}\cdot K.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the spatial dimension of patches at scale <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{l}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{l}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the number of tokens per scale (<span id="A1.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span>, a <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{l}\times L_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{l}\times L_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> patch grid contains <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{l}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{l}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> tokens).
The denominator <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{K}L_{k}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{K}L_{k}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> normalizes the token counts across all scales, ensuring that finer-grained resolutions (larger <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>) are not overshadowed by coarser ones (smaller <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>). This ensures the model prioritizes dynamic regions over static ones, which are more likely to change across frames.
Such a weighted strategy is essential for capturing the underlying spatial patterns in robot-centric world modeling, leading to more effective learning.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> 1X Dataset Preprocessing Pipeline</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            Dataset root paths <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{train}},\mathcal{D}_{\text{val}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>train</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>val</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{train}},\mathcal{D}_{\text{val}}</annotation></semantics></math>, Target frame rate <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math>, Minimum segment length <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{min}}=51" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>51</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{min}}=51</annotation></semantics></math>, Clip length <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{clip}}=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>clip</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{clip}}=30</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            Joint index mapping <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}:\{0,\dots,24\}\rightarrow\{\text{HIP\_YAW},\dots,\text{Angular Velocity}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>24</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext>HIP_YAW</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Angular Velocity</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}:\{0,\dots,24\}\rightarrow\{\text{HIP\_YAW},\dots,\text{Angular Velocity}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">repeat</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M},\mathcal{S},\mathcal{R},\mathcal{V}\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>train</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M},\mathcal{S},\mathcal{R},\mathcal{V}\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{train}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Load metadata, segment indices, robot states, and video frames</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S},\mathcal{R},\mathcal{V}\leftarrow\text{Downsample}(\mathcal{S},\mathcal{R},\mathcal{V},\delta f=\left\lfloor\frac{30}{f_{\text{target}}}\right\rfloor)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>Downsample</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mfrac><mn>30</mn><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub></mfrac><mo>⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S},\mathcal{R},\mathcal{V}\leftarrow\text{Downsample}(\mathcal{S},\mathcal{R},\mathcal{V},\delta f=\left\lfloor\frac{30}{f_{\text{target}}}\right\rfloor)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l5.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Temporal downsampling</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}\leftarrow\text{UniqueSegments}(\mathcal{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>UniqueSegments</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}\leftarrow\text{UniqueSegments}(\mathcal{S})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Extract unique action segments</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for all</span> <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{start}},\tau_{\text{end}}\leftarrow\text{FindBounds}(\mathcal{S}=s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>start</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>end</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>FindBounds</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{start}},\tau_{\text{end}}\leftarrow\text{FindBounds}(\mathcal{S}=s)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Segment boundary detection</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{end}}-\tau_{\text{start}}&lt;T_{\text{min}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>end</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>start</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{end}}-\tau_{\text{start}}&lt;T_{\text{min}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
                 <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">continue</span> <span id="alg1.l10.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l10.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Skip short segments</span>
</span>
</div>
